WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
Start with a yellow solution
of vanadium in acid.

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:06.660
Add a few pieces of
another metal, and swirl.

3
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.380
The yellow turns blue.

4
00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:09.500
Then green.

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.720
Then violet.

6
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:14.320
Four shades, one metal, one flask.

7
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.620
So how can one metal give
four different shades,

8
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.380
one after another, in the same flask?

9
00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:23.340
In this mission, you'll learn
the shades of chromium,

10
00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:28.440
manganese and iron ions in solution,
from purple to very pale pink.

11
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:33.800
Then you'll choose reagents that carry a metal
from one shade to another, and back again.

12
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.770
Your mission: explain how one metal
can give four shades in one flask.